# Build artifacts
*.obj
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll

# Every project's build output (objects, .d files, executables, archives)
# lives under a project-anchored build/ dir. Anchored (not a bare `build/`)
# so this can never shadow the vendored, committed .a files under
# third_party/ (see the raylib/box3d exceptions below) — git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so a bare `build/` rule would make
# those unrecoverable by negation.
/MatterEngine3/build/
/MatterEngine3/tests/build/
/MatterEditor/build/
/libs/*/build/
# The single-segment `*` above stops at libs/<name>/build/ and does not reach
# into libs/<name>/tests/build/ (a separate, independently-Makefiled build
# dir that MatterSurfaceLib and MeshChartingLib each have) — one more level
# needed here.
/libs/*/tests/build/

# Per-project compiled binaries (named after the project)
BasicWindowApp/cube_app
SurfaceLib/surface_app
OpenParticleSurfaceLib/open_particle_surface
GPURayTraceExample/gpu_raytrace
GPURayTraceExample/shader_preprocessor
ParticleDynamicsExample/particle_dynamics

# Misc
SurfaceLib/test_config
*.ini

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Claude Code / assistant tool state (regenerated locally)
.claude/

# Allow raylib's vendored static lib through the *.a exclusion (committed builds)
!third_party/raylib/build/**/libraylib.a
!third_party/raylib/src/libraylib.a

# Vendored TBB (third_party/autoremesher_core/thirdparty/tbb) ships its own
# build system under `build/` -- the .inc / Makefile source files there are
# NOT artifacts and must be tracked. Un-ignore the whole tree, then re-ignore
# the versioned per-config build output subdirs it emits at build time.
!third_party/autoremesher_core/thirdparty/tbb/build/
!third_party/autoremesher_core/thirdparty/tbb/build/**
third_party/autoremesher_core/thirdparty/tbb/build/linux_*_debug/
third_party/autoremesher_core/thirdparty/tbb/build/linux_*_release/
third_party/autoremesher_core/thirdparty/tbb/build/*_debug/
third_party/autoremesher_core/thirdparty/tbb/build/*_release/
# Allow box3d's prebuilt Linux and MinGW static libs
!third_party/box3d/libbox3d.a
!third_party/box3d/build-mingw/libbox3d.a

# MatterEngine3 compiled binaries and bake caches
MatterEngine3/tests/*_check
MatterEngine3/tests/*_profile
MatterEngine3/tests/example_world
MatterEngine3/tests/*.log
MatterEngine3/tests/sandbox/

# viewer-integration tests (share viewer's object graph; live in viewer/ for
# now — see followup on moving to tests/)

# autoremesher_core smoke-test binaries (compiled from same-named drivers)
third_party/autoremesher_core/tests/smoke_cube
third_party/autoremesher_core/tests/quad_to_tri_test

# `make TARGET=linux` (build-all.sh convention) emits a binary named `linux`
libs/MemoryLib/linux
libs/SpatialQueryLib/linux

# Transient screenshots + sentinel files (FIFO shot capture)
*.png.done
MatterEngine3/tools/shots_task6/
shots/
# (no trailing slash: shaders is a symlink in fresh checkouts, a dir otherwise)

# Local backups / imposter test outputs / world bake data
*.bak
imposters/

# Bake artifacts (Phase 1, repo-layout-and-cache-consolidation): every
# "parts" and "cache" directory the engine or its tooling produces is
# confined to <project_dir>/.cache/<world_name>/parts (see
# LocalProviderConfig::for_project in MatterEngine3/src/provider/
# local_provider.h and EngineContext::create in
# MatterEngine3/src/matter_engine.cpp, both fixed to require/derive an
# absolute cache_root instead of defaulting to a bare relative "cache").
# These two bare patterns match at any depth and replace what used to be
# location-specific rules for MatterEngine3/viewer/cache,
# libs/MatterSurfaceLib/parts, MatterEngine3/tests/parts/, MatterEditor/cache,
# MatterEngine3/parts, and a bare `parts` — several of which existed only
# because of the relative-path bug that fix closes. `cache/` (no dot) is
# still needed: Bake Lab's scratch directory (MatterEditor/src/part_workbench.cpp
# scratch_root_ = "cache/lab-scratch") is intentionally relative/ephemeral
# and out of this fix's scope.
parts
cache/
.cache/

# Screenshots/ is a checked-in folder — override the broad `shots/` rule above
# for the specific subdir that happens to be named `shots`.
!Screenshots/shots/
.outrider
.worktrees/
.superpowers/sdd/review-*.diff

# Blanket safety net. The per-project /build/ rules below express the LAYOUT we
# want; these express what must never be committed anywhere, including legacy
# directories (MatterEngine3/viewer), vendored trees that build in place
# (third_party/box3d, third_party/autoremesher_core) and scratch dirs (.tmp).
# Removing these in favour of the anchored rules alone let `git add -A` sweep
# 60 MB of stale artifacts into a commit. `*.a` is deliberately NOT blanket:
# two vendored archives are legitimately tracked (see the negations below).
*.o
*.d
*.exe
.tmp/

# NOTE -- stray extensionless files with random 8-character names (e.g.
# `stcjVZme`) appearing beside sources are GCC/assembler temporaries, not
# source. MSYS2's make clobbers the Windows TEMP variable, so a build run
# WITHOUT `TMP=... TEMP=...` passed as make VARIABLES (see CLAUDE.md) drops the
# compiler's scratch into the working directory. They are always safe to
# delete. Deliberately NOT ignored by pattern: any glob broad enough to catch a
# random 8-char name also silently swallows legitimate files, and a stray file
# visible in `git status` is a better failure than a real file silently ignored.

# Junction guard (Windows). MatterEngine3/shaders, MatterEditor/shaders and
# MatterEditor/shaders_gpu are tracked SYMLINKS (mode 120000). With
# core.symlinks=false they exist in the working tree as NTFS junctions, so a
# `git add <parent-dir>` descends INTO them and stages the target's files as new
# blobs -- silently replacing each symlink with a directory of duplicates. The
# skip-worktree bit does not prevent this (the new paths differ from the flagged
# one). These trailing-slash rules match the DIRECTORY only, so git stops
# descending; the already-tracked symlink entries are unaffected because ignore
# rules never apply to tracked paths.
/MatterEngine3/shaders/
/MatterEditor/shaders/
/MatterEditor/shaders_gpu/

# Built in place by build-all.sh; not vendored (unlike box3d, negated above).
/third_party/autoremesher_core/libautoremesher_core.a
